CHAPTER THREE
PROJECT IMPLEMENTATION
3.0 Introduction
This chapter describes the implementation of the Climate-Smart Improved Kienyeji Chicken Broiler Production Enterprise at St. Mary's Girls Secondary School – Thigio. It outlines the practical activities undertaken from project establishment to the marketing stage, including housing preparation, chick procurement, brooding, feeding, health management, climate-smart practices, record keeping, monitoring, and evaluation.
The project was implemented by twenty-four Agriculture candidates organized into five working groups under the supervision of the Agriculture teacher. Each group participated in all production activities through a rotational work schedule to ensure that every learner acquired practical skills in poultry production and enterprise management.
The project commenced with 60 day-old improved Kienyeji chicks. During the production period, 9 birds died, leaving 51 birds, representing an 85% survival rate.
